---
import Base from "@/layouts/Base.astro";
import Navigation from "@/components/Navigation";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import founders from "@/assets/founders.jpg";
---

<Base
  title="About the studio"
  description="DOCA Architecture & Design was founded in 2024 by Ștefan Diaconescu and Vlad Căpitanu, combining BIM and project management with Scandinavian urban design practice."
  breadcrumb="About"
>
  <div class="min-h-screen bg-background">
    <Navigation client:load />

    <main class="pt-32 pb-16">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-8">
        <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-light text-text-primary text-center mb-12">
          About Our Studio
        </h1>

        <figure class="mb-16">
          <Image
            src={founders}
            alt="Vlad Căpitanu and Ștefan Diaconescu, founders of DOCA Architecture & Design"
            widths={[480, 768, 1024]}
            sizes="(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 768px"
            format="avif"
            class="w-full h-auto"
          />
          <figcaption class="mt-3 text-center text-sm text-text-tertiary">
            Vlad Căpitanu and Ștefan Diaconescu
          </figcaption>
        </figure>

        <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-8">
          <p class="text-lg text-text-secondary leading-relaxed text-justify">
            DOCA Architecture &amp; Design is a Romania-based architecture practice, founded in
            2024 by
            <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/stefandiaconescu" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
               class="font-medium text-text-primary hover:text-accent-hover transition-colors duration-200">Ștefan Diaconescu</a>
            and
            <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/vlad-capitanu-12850b1ab" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
               class="font-medium text-text-primary hover:text-accent-hover transition-colors duration-200">Vlad Căpitanu</a>.
          </p>

          <p class="text-lg text-text-secondary leading-relaxed text-justify">
            Our long-standing professional collaboration naturally evolved into establishing
            DOCA, building on a series of early joint projects and international competitions.
            From the outset, our work has engaged with diverse scales, with a strong emphasis on
            space efficiency, usability, urban integration, and human-scale architecture.
          </p>

          <p class="text-lg text-text-secondary leading-relaxed text-justify">
            At the core of our philosophy lies the experience of the end-user. We place the
            individual at the center of the architectural process, designing spaces that are not
            only functional but also sculptural— living environments shaped to enrich daily life.
          </p>

          <section class="text-lg text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
            <h2 class="font-semibold mb-4 text-text-primary">Selected Competitions &amp; Projects</h2>
            <ul class="space-y-1">
              <li>Central Park Book Studio – New York, 2019</li>
              <li>Weave – Sustainable Fashion Hub – Milan, 2019</li>
              <li>City Link – Copenhagen, 2020</li>
              <li>Roots – MilanCall – Milan, 2020 (2nd Prize)</li>
            </ul>
          </section>

          <section class="text-lg text-text-secondary leading-relaxed text-justify">
            <h2 class="font-semibold mb-4 text-text-primary">Our Complementary Professional Paths</h2>
            <ul class="space-y-4">
              <li>
                <span class="font-medium">Ștefan Diaconescu</span> refined his expertise in BIM
                management and project management, with a focus on problem-solving, site
                coordination, and technical detailing. His ongoing research into technical
                solutions continuously enhances the quality and innovation of our work.
              </li>
              <li>
                <span class="font-medium">Vlad Căpitanu</span> deepened his architectural
                perspective through a Master's degree in Sustainable Urban Planning and Design at
                KTH, Sweden. His Scandinavian experience—both academic and professional—shapes his
                design philosophy, emphasizing scale, materiality, sustainability, and geometry.
              </li>
            </ul>
          </section>

          <p class="text-lg text-text-secondary leading-relaxed text-justify">
            DOCA represents the synthesis of these experiences—a balance between technical
            precision and conceptual vision. We believe architecture should be human-centered,
            creating spaces that respond to both individual and collective needs while
            integrating seamlessly into their cultural and urban contexts.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </main>
  </div>
</Base>
